  "id": "Compound::DB04920 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Clevidipine is shown to bind to Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase and (s)-limonene 6-monooxygenase activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2c19, suggesting a potential role for Cyp2c9 in the regulation of Cyp2c19 function. The shared pathway from Clevidipine to Cyp2c9 and then to Cyp2c19 implies that Clevidipine may influence Cyp2c19 through a mechanism involving Cyp2c9. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Clevidipine and Cyp2c19, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action and its biological relevance.",
